# Tailwind v4 + Preline UI

## Tailwind v4

- This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4** via `@tailwindcss/vite` with a config-less setup. Brand tokens are declared in `@theme` blocks inside `app/assets/css/main.css` and `landing.css`.
- Brand-extended utilities available: `bg-brand-purple`, `bg-brand-green`, `bg-brand-orange`, `bg-paper`, `bg-ink`, `font-display`, `font-mono`, plus the standard Tailwind utilities.
- Use tokens, not arbitrary values. Bad: `text-[#8B5CF6]`. Good: `text-brand-purple`.
- Dark mode is class-based (`dark:`). Always pair light/dark variants.
- Mobile-first responsive: write base classes for mobile, then `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` overrides.

## Preline UI

Preline is the chosen interactive primitive library. Use it whenever a component needs JS-driven state (open/close, focus trap, ARIA wiring).

### When to Reach for Preline

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Dropdown menus | Preline `hs-dropdown` |
| Modals / dialogs | Preline `hs-overlay` |
| Tabs | Preline `hs-tab` |
| Carousels | Preline `hs-carousel` |
| Tooltips | Preline `hs-tooltip` |
| Comboboxes / search | Preline `hs-combobox` |
| Simple accordion (FAQ) | Native `<details>` (per brand guide §11) |

### Initialization

Preline must be initialized **once** in a Nuxt client plugin (e.g. `app/plugins/preline.client.ts`). Never import or re-init inside individual components.

```ts
// app/plugins/preline.client.ts
import "preline/preline";

export default defineNuxtPlugin(() => {
  // Preline auto-binds on DOMContentLoaded; trigger on route change too.
});
```

### Styling Preline Primitives

- Always restyle with brand Tailwind classes — never ship Preline's default theme.
- Preserve required `hs-*` data attributes and class hooks; layer brand styles on top.

```html
<div class="hs-dropdown relative inline-flex">
  <button
    class="hs-dropdown-toggle inline-flex items-center gap-2
           bg-brand-purple text-white px-6 py-3.5 rounded-full
           hover:bg-ink hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all"
  >
    Options
  </button>
  <div class="hs-dropdown-menu hidden ... rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-white/10 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 shadow-soft">
    ...
  </div>
</div>
```

### Don'ts

- Don't pair Preline with another UI framework (Headless UI, Radix, Nuxt UI) — pick one.
- Don't use Preline's default purple/blue theme — always override with brand tokens.
- Don't re-implement Preline behaviors with custom JS when the primitive exists.

## Class Order (Conventional)

`layout → positioning → display → spacing → sizing → typography → colors → borders → effects → transitions → states (`hover:`, `focus:`, `dark:`)` — keep readability over strict order, but group related utilities.
